# NetraVerse ML

This folder contains the training and evaluation side of the passive
threat-detection system.

It does not contain packet datasets. Capture data and generated feature
files should stay outside Git.

## Architecture

1. Capture authorized lab traffic into PCAP files.
2. Record capture and scenario IDs so test data can be separated by scenario.
3. Use the service's offline feature extractor to create a labelled feature CSV.
4. Train six separate binary XGBoost models.
5. Select each decision threshold using validation data.
6. Evaluate once on held-out test scenarios.
7. Export XGBoost JSON models and thresholds for C++ inference.

The Python feature names are defined in `feature_schema.py`. The C++ feature
extractor must compute these same features using the same definitions and
time windows.

